@startuml
hide footbox
title Shared ideas — hand-editing the AI-enhanced document
actor Admin
participant "Ideas AI document services" as API
database "MySQL: media results\n(editable_document_json)" as DB
participant "IdeaTiptapDocxProvider\n(ideas-only converter)" as Docx
participant "LibreOffice (PDF conversion)" as PDF
participant "Media service / S3" as S3

== Open the editor ==
Admin -> API : GET /:id/ai-enhancement/medias/:sourceMediaId/document
API -> DB : Current attempt + media result (DOCUMENT, ENHANCED)
alt editable_document_json stored
 API --> Admin : 200 {document, source: STORED, editedAt}
else older result without JSON
 API -> S3 : Download enhanced PDF (owned URL)
 API -> API : Extract text -> one paragraph per line
 API --> Admin : 200 {document, source: EXTRACTED}
end

== Generate the PDF ==
Admin -> API : PUT same path {enhancementId, document}
API -> API : Validate (shape, known nodes, depth, size, not empty)\n422 IDEA_AI_8629 otherwise
API -> DB : Fail fast: attempt is current? result editable? (409 / 404)
API -> Docx : TipTap JSON -> DOCX
API -> PDF : DOCX -> PDF
API -> S3 : Upload new PDF + DOCX (tracked)
API -> DB : Transaction: lock idea
alt published / AI working / attempt no longer current
 API -> DB : Rollback
 API -> S3 : Discard the new uploads (unreferenced)
 API --> Admin : 409
else ok
 API -> DB : New media items; result points to them;\nsave JSON + document_edited_at
 API -> DB : Old items deleted only if no other attempt result uses them
 API -> S3 : After commit: delete old files no media row references
 API --> Admin : 200 {document, source: STORED, editedAt}
end
note over API : The AI essence guard does not run on a human edit.
@enduml
